1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,777
Hell Pass!

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:04,020
Hell Pass! Dream State!

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,117
Hell Pass !Hell Pass!

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,180
Hell Pass!

5
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:52,717
All of

6
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:29,820
Heaps ya!

7
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:35,870
Heaps!

8
00:01:35,953 --> 00:01:36,880
Heaps ya!

9
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:40,617
Seems I've climbed aboard a
ship with a storm for a captain!

10
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,530
Bah!

11
00:01:41,613 --> 00:01:42,443
What luck I have!

12
00:01:42,526 --> 00:01:45,045
You certainly are a
handful, aren't you, Luffy?

13
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,190
I love it!

14
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,200
Your dream is great!

15
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,220
I love it! Oh, yeah?

16
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:53,680
I'm so happy!

17
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,060
Oh, hey, easy there, buddy!

18
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,640
Crazy, but it's just perfect for you.

19
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:01,757
No way that's gonna happen until
you're King of the Pirates, though.

20
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,016
Better get cracking.

21
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,520
One more road poneglyph to Laugh Tale.

22
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:08,058
We're in the homestretch, everybody!

23
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:10,928
Perhaps so, but it won't
be an easy stretch.

24
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,717
We have a dangerous journey ahead.

25
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:16,506
The last road Poneglyph will be
the most difficult one to find.

26
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,760
Not to mention, we don't have
a single lead to follow up on.

27
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:28,486
Unlike the others, no one has
been able to find this Poneglyph.

28
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,400
We're sailing straight
into uncharted waters.

29
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,220
It's Flame Emperor Sabo!

30
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:48,197
He's calling the Kamabaka Queendom!

31
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,110
Good!

32
00:02:49,193 --> 00:02:50,200
We'll hunt him down!

33
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,168
Let's trace that call, men!

34
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,937
The signal's not being jammed.

35
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:54,877
That's strange.

36
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,817
Why isn't he using a white
transponder snail to keep us out?

37
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,700
It must be an emergency call!

38
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:01,097
We better make this quick!

39
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,945
We need to get his location
before he hangs up!

40
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,020
We can't let this leak go!

41
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:17,360
The trace was successful.
Where is it from?

42
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,920
The kingdom of Lulusia.

43
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,300
From Lulusia.

44
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:25,040
Well, well.

45
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,757
We've been informed that
the insurgents in Lulusia

46
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,977
successfully overthrew
the country's monarchy.

47
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:32,297
at the start of the
Eight Nation Revolution.

48
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:34,733
It's the perfect place for Sabo to hide.

49
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:36,740
Then it's settled.

50
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,002
Sabo's quite the unlucky fellow.

51
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,840
It's not luck.

52
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,620
This is his destiny.

53
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,540
I'm fine.

54
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,292
Just glad I got through.

55
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,240
I'm glad too.

56
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,440
Yeah, me too!

57
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,737
But you sure took your sweet time calling!

58
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:02,177
What was the big hold-up?

59
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:04,237
Darling, I've been worried sick about you!

60
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,237
How can you do this to your dear friend?

61
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,560
I'm sorry, everyone.

62
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,900
You stop that!

63
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:11,236
You stop the police asking right now!

64
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,797
I have a feeling it's a
bit too early to celebrate.

65
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:17,637
You didn't call just to let
us know you're alive, did you?

66
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,073
So, what's the lowdown?

67
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,600
For starters, you read the article, right?

68
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:26,389
So you probably have
some questions for me.

69
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,190
Dragon.

70
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:37,820
It's true that King Cobra is dead.

71
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,780
I didn't kill him.

72
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,780
I knew it!

73
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,677
We never doubted you, Sabo!

74
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,700
We always believed in
you by innocent love!

75
00:04:56,340 --> 00:05:00,800
Before I fled from Marie Joie, I
saw something I still can't believe.

76
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,940
What did you see, Sabo?

77
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,720
What's going on?

78
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,437
Never seen clouds like that.

79
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,000
No, that isn't a cloud.

80
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:38,818
There's something floating up there.

81
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,700
You insects will pay for this treachery!

82
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:45,817
You think the navy won't hear of this?

83
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:48,597
They'll burn you at the stake
and entail what's left of you!

84
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,915
Father, let me scold the traitors too!

85
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,320
Prepare to be eradicated, vermin!

86
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,660
Lord Zeki, please just listen!

87
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:58,877
This revolt has been a long
time coming, can't you see?

88
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:02,717
This wouldn't have happened if you
had thought of your people's welfare!

89
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,630
What?!

90
00:06:03,713 --> 00:06:07,197
Why should the king waste his time
thinking about a bunch of lonely pedants?

91
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:09,617
You know your place, you insolent worms!

92
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,837
All we want is for you
to admit your wrongs!

93
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,979
Please, my lord, we won't
hurt you, I swear, just...

94
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:17,940
Get me out of this cage. No!

95
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:37,852
I was still at the reverie at
the time, in Pangaea Castle.

96
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,000
And I saw the empty throne.

97
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:44,100
Communications, cut off
your transponder snail. Huh?

98
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:46,420
Do I need to repeat myself?

99
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,470
Sorry, sir.

100
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:52,137
They always say that there's
no king of the world,

101
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:54,279
so no one is supposed to sit there.

102
00:06:57,540 --> 00:06:59,481
Communications, listen carefully.

103
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:12,780
You did not trace any calls
today, do you understand?

104
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,475
Yeah, but I'm scared!

105
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:24,400
You didn't overhear a single word.

106
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:30,080
And as for Lulucyan...

107
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:38,340
I've never heard of it.

108
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,060
In fact, it never existed.

109
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,380
What's happening now?

110
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,690
Sabo?

111
00:08:37,773 --> 00:08:38,603
Are you there?

112
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:49,585
A major Squad just hit
up the southeast coast!

113
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,367
Make emergency preparations!

114
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:52,760
A tsunami is coming!

115
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,360
We're all going to die!

116
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,000
It's freezing!

117
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,760
This is a nightmare!

118
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:25,180
Someone help!

119
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,350
Don't kill me again!

120
00:09:26,433 --> 00:09:27,555
We talked about this!

121
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,840
What kind of madness is this?

122
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:52,377
Hey, aren't you cold without a shirt on?

123
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,290
I'm fine.

124
00:09:53,373 --> 00:09:55,117
Feeling hot or cold is all in your head.

125
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,030
Oh, I see.

126
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:59,117
So your head's well insulated
because it's full of moss.

127
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,030
What's that?

128
00:10:00,113 --> 00:10:01,520
You think you're cold?

129
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:02,877
Wait till I throw you in the ocean!

130
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,019
Let's see you try!

131
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,181
Could you two possibly
take a worse time to argue?

132
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,350
Jeep A!

133
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,120
Watch out for icebergs! Roger!

134
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:25,760
Furl the sails quickly!

135
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,377
The winds are far too strong!

136
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,754
Oh, you heard the man.

137
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:29,880
Let's go!

138
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:37,960
Strong run!

139
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:49,300
Take up the pace, Mosshead!

140
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,297
You're holding me back!

141
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:53,615
You really like the sound of
your own voice, don't you?

142
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,068
Tommy, do you see any land?

143
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:01,398
No, not yet, but we should
come up on an island soon.

144
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:05,957
With this snow, I'm assuming we're
probably within range of a winter island.

145
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,099
And it must be one with an
especially harsh climate.

146
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,897
Seems like they're having a hard time.

147
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,920
I'd better go help. How cute.

148
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:21,300
I love the hat. Looking good.

149
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:26,540
With this woven headpiece
that Otama bestowed upon me,

150
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,915
the falling snow shall prove no peril.

151
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:35,980
Hey, Nami!

152
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,700
Don't get this out!

153
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,380
Yeah, what?

154
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,717
What is that thing?

155
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:54,280
Looks like a warm eddy of
considerable size! No way!

156
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:57,160
That's an eddy! Oh, great! What now?

157
00:11:57,860 --> 00:11:59,180
That thing's huge!

158
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:02,500
How is an eddy floating
in the air like that?

159
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,030
Concentratedly!

160
00:12:04,113 --> 00:12:07,017
It must have warmed up so much
that it rose above the sea!

161
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,800
There's no way that's right!

162
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:13,417
Like a big, beautiful afro...

163
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:14,500
Get away, Jinpei!

164
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:15,780
It'll suck us in!

165
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,740
Leave it to me! Wait!

166
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,706
There's someone floating
up there in the water

167
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:23,640
Oh, what?

168
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,357
You think there's a mermaid?

169
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,540
Whoa, what's that?

170
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,537
I think Loopy's right.

171
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:37,557
I heard a little girl crying out.

172
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,464
You heard that from underwater?

173
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:44,300
What the hell's going on?

174
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,640
Even if there is someone, what can we do?

175
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,940
I'll just cut him out.

176
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:04,960
If you put so much as a scratch on that
girl, I swear I'm going to fillet your ass.

177
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,179
Like I would miss.

178
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:18,620
Here we go.

179
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:28,240
One sword style.

180
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:29,740
Bird dance!

181
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:35,980
Recapi-e!

182
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:43,680
Itings, comrades! I heard
a fuss. What ails thee?

183
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:44,737
Worry not!

184
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:47,960
Well, then hat-jumper-ay-man is here to...

185
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,260
To ensure our stuff!

186
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,832
Why did you stay inside?

187
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:55,497
You had it all and you
threw it all the way!

188
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:56,410
Stop it!

189
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,380
Hold on!

190
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:04,460
Thanks, Lupi!

191
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:09,240
Oh, give me a break, not you two!

192
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,537
What the hell are they doing?

193
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:12,540
Come on!

194
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,880
There's a little kid up there!

195
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:30,580
Who is that?

196
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:40,020
Who's there?

197
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,937
Thank you.

198
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,080
Where's the monster?

199
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,620
She's okay.

200
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,897
That's a relief. But, uh...

201
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:52,897
They're kind of just floating
up there, aren't they?

202
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:54,080
Hold up.

203
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,712
She's yelling something.

204
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:58,290
Stop!

205
00:14:58,373 --> 00:14:59,480
Look down!

206
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:01,920
She said look down.

207
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:11,620
What is that thing?

208
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:22,860
We need to get out of here now, sail away!

209
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:40,920
Is this how it ends for us?

210
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,520
Jinbei! Hurry!

211
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:45,280
Come on, Jinbei!

212
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,300
Step on it! Let's go!

213
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:49,091
You can't leave it to me!

214
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,320
Move it!

215
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,440
What the hell is that thing?

216
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,517
I thought it was a shark,
but it's way too big.

217
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,776
And it looks like it's made of metal!

218
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,340
Hold on tight!

219
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,386
We're about to hit the water!

220
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:22,080
This isn't cool!

221
00:16:22,420 --> 00:16:24,057
They fell straight into the sea!

222
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:25,180
I need to go now!

223
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:27,450
Franky!

224
00:16:27,533 --> 00:16:28,540
Take the helm for me!

225
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,260
I'm going after them!

226
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:32,260
Bring the ship around to us!

227
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,360
No problem!

228
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,835
I got your back, bro!

229
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:48,900
I said no problem, but
these waters are rough.

230
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,257
We can't find them.

231
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,600
Well, I got some tricks up my sleeve.

232
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,100
Ship's bottom!

233
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:08,740
Rapid screw!

234
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:12,960
Up to it, baby!

235
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:21,950
Alright!

236
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:25,024
Frankie's coming for you,
bros, don't you worry!

237
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:40,140
Luffy! Chopper!

238
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:42,600
Stupid snow! I can't see!

239
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:51,440
Freaky! Move!

240
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:53,380
We got torpedoes!

241
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,440
Help me! Love me!

242
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,300
Oh, crap!

243
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:06,500
It's gonna capsize!

244
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:27,084
It sounded like there was
an explosion up above.

245
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:32,720
Chobro, move it.

246
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:34,260
I'm almost there.

247
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,206
You're going to be all right.

248
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,927
We're nearly to the surface.

249
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:46,236
You'll be safe soon.

250
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,040
I won't let you die.

251
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,460
This current is far too strong.

252
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,915
The Sunny can't navigate through this.

253
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:01,610
Thanks, Jimmy.

254
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:02,900
You saved us.

255
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,394
Well, there's no need to worry anymore.

256
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:11,202
Now we just have to find
our way back to the sun.

257
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:28,920
Nothing wrong, GP.

258
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,620
Hold on, charge.

259
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,517
We'll head for the seafloor.

260
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:39,071
Everyone take a deep breath while you can!

261
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:40,339
We're going under!

262
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,540
Here we go!

263
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:10,830
Damn it!

264
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,668
The current's way too fast!

265
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:13,940
We can't surface!

266
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,680
We're all gonna drown!

267
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,380
Why am I into water?

268
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:20,297
What the hell's going on?!

269
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:21,960
Hang in there, Robin!

270
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:24,650
Nami!

271
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,700
This ain't good.

272
00:21:19,060 --> 00:21:21,236
We gotta come up with something fast.

273
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:24,080
Though we're all dead.

274
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:40,497
Hi, everyone.

275
00:21:40,580 --> 00:21:41,420
I'm back.

276
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,962
Are you ready for your medicine?

277
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,920
One cup each.

278
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,000
Drink it up.

279
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:51,420
Okay, fine.

280
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:54,266
I'm gonna drink it, but
only for you, Toshiki.

281
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:55,960
That's a good boy.

282
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,737
Sorry, guys, but you'll have
to drink every last drop.

283
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,200
This tastes weird.

284
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:04,260
It's gross. I hate it.
Be brave. You can do it.

285
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:08,160
Do I really gotta drink the whole glass?

286
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,157
Yeah, then you'll turn
back to your normal size.

287
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:14,534
All right, if you say it'll
fix me, then I'll drink too.

288
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:15,750
Tashigi!

289
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:17,199
What do you think?

290
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,359
Do I look smaller?

291
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:21,420
You look great, Mock. It's working.

292
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:24,560
Does that mean I can go home soon? Uh-huh.

293
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,617
Just keep up the good work.

294
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:27,876
You're almost there.

295
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:29,090
Tashigi!

296
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,860
Vice Admiral Dole.

297
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:33,880
Can I borrow you for a sec?

298
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:39,460
Helmepo is driving everyone crazy.

299
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,797
Come on, can you please talk to him?

300
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:44,320
Look, I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

301
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:47,557
He has every right to be
worried about his friend.

302
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:48,880
And I see why.

303
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:51,629
We all wish we could
do something for Kobe.

304
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,537
Do something for Kobe!

305
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:57,760
He's our brother in arms,
but we can't let him die!

306
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,840
Both of us are on our knees begging you.

307
00:23:01,340 --> 00:23:02,987
Gobi has been so good to me.

308
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,806
He deserves better than this.

309
00:23:05,020 --> 00:23:08,079
We have to go to Pirate
Island before it's too late.

310
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,102
Please, Prince.

311
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:14,640
If you won't help us, we'll
have to go by ourselves.

312
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:20,060
Please have a heart.

313
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:24,917
I'm sorry, but I won't move an
inch until you promise to help us.

314
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:29,340
If you really expect to waltz into
Blackbeard's turf and come back alive,

315
00:23:29,660 --> 00:23:32,072
you'd be picking a fight with an emperor.

316
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:36,100
Place is a death trap.

317
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:39,740
You poke the hive and
you're gonna get swarmed.

318
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:44,200
A whole horde of bloodthirsty
pirates will shoot you up.

319
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,776
That's why they call it Full of Lead.

320
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:53,512
Egghead's pretty close to here, you know.

321
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:57,340
We can take the seraphim, too!

322
00:23:57,860 --> 00:23:59,200
You've lost your mind.

323
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,720
No way in hell, okay?

324
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:02,880
Let's all just calm down.

325
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:08,840
I wish we could contact
Drake with that shot, too.

326
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,620
There's nothing we can do.

327
00:24:16,780 --> 00:24:18,080
Try to understand.

328
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,070
Kobe!

329
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:31,197
What you seriously don't know who I am?

330
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:33,017
Nope, no clue.

331
00:24:33,100 --> 00:24:35,197
We're both part of the worst generation.

332
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:38,157
Stupid—did you just forget
me or everyone else too?

333
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,937
Oh, cool, you're the worst too. Huh, nice.

334
00:24:41,020 --> 00:24:41,850
Don't

335
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,677
say it like that, you idiot!

336
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:44,590
idiot

337
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:50,376
I was there at Sabaody, too,
you know, two years back.

338
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:52,940
The name is Bonnie.

339
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:55,300
We're rivals. You got that?

340
00:24:56,260 --> 00:24:58,940
That aside, you still saved my life.

341
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:01,060
So thanks for that.

342
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:04,120
Aw, hey, don't mention it, Bonnie.

343
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:05,760
Bonnie, damn it!

344
00:25:05,900 --> 00:25:07,560
Cut that out, Luffy!

345
00:25:10,820 --> 00:25:11,760
Stop it!

346
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:12,860
It's cold!

347
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:16,300
Now I'm immune to your wicked waterways.

348
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:19,160
Well, I'm immune to your immunity. Watch!

349
00:25:20,380 --> 00:25:21,860
This guy is an emperor?

350
00:25:25,660 --> 00:25:28,700
By the way, why is your
wanted poster so weird?

351
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:30,941
I thought your hair turned white.

352
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:33,452
The newspapers made a big deal out of it.

353
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:35,020
Oh, yeah? That's funny.

354
00:25:37,860 --> 00:25:40,497
That's just how I look
when I'm totally free.

355
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:41,657
Oh, forget I asked.

356
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:43,577
So what happened to your friends?

357
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:44,778
Think they're okay?

358
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,060
I'm sure they're fine.

359
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:51,360
And what about your crew?

360
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:53,953
I didn't see your ship out there either.

361
00:25:55,060 --> 00:25:56,820
I came here alone.

362
00:25:57,780 --> 00:26:01,100
As for my ship, it got gobbled
up by that giant monster.

363
00:26:01,980 --> 00:26:03,320
Stupid metal bastard.

364
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,000
I'm sorry to hear it.

365
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:08,900
Man, I really gotta find me some grub.

366
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:13,320
Actually, I'm hungry too.

367
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:15,520
No good place to eat.

368
00:26:16,460 --> 00:26:17,290
Good idea.

369
00:26:17,373 --> 00:26:20,125
Let's find some money
and head to a restaurant.

370
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:21,130
What?

371
00:26:21,213 --> 00:26:22,276
Are you guys stupid?

372
00:26:22,580 --> 00:26:24,227
There's no restaurants here.

373
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:28,800
This island belongs to the government.

374
00:26:31,060 --> 00:26:32,640
Let me fill you in.

375
00:26:33,020 --> 00:26:36,440
They call this place Egghead Island. Dr.

376
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:38,997
Vegapunk's lab is here, and
thanks to his inventions,

377
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:42,540
they say this island is
500 years in the future.

378
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:45,400
Dr. Vegapunk?

379
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:47,207
I've heard that name before.

380
00:26:50,100 --> 00:26:52,453
I'm here to give him a piece of my mind.

381
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:54,080
We've got business.

382
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:12,300
Is everyone here? Are you all right?

383
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:18,120
Did the Sonny survive all that?

384
00:27:27,540 --> 00:27:28,370
It's...

385
00:27:28,453 --> 00:27:29,283
it's...

386
00:27:29,366 --> 00:27:30,900
The giant robot!

387
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,360
But who is operating it?

388
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:49,117
Careful here, they come.

389
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:51,357
That was a bust.

390
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:54,897
Where did I go wrong this time?

391
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:59,737
Guess, I can't code the
instincts out of a living thing.

392
00:27:59,820 --> 00:28:04,377
Whatever, I'll work on that. I don't.

393
00:28:04,460 --> 00:28:06,037
I don't know who you are, but thanks!

394
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:07,420
You saved our asses!

395
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:08,800
I owe you one!

396
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:10,430
Hardly.

397
00:28:10,513 --> 00:28:12,987
I'm just here to
troubleshoot my mecha-shark.

398
00:28:17,740 --> 00:28:20,837
All I ordered that hunky-junk
to do was scout, report,

399
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:25,214
and bombard, not eat the target and
destroy all their frickin' valuables.

400
00:28:25,820 --> 00:28:27,467
Must be a programming error.

401
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:37,670
What?!

402
00:28:37,753 --> 00:28:40,696
You filthy pirates really
thought I came to save you?!

403
00:28:40,980 --> 00:28:45,560
A genius government scientist like me
has no business with the likes of you!

404
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:51,660
My name is Dr. Vegapunk!

405
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:56,870
What?!

406
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:18,437
Thank

407
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:19,837
you

408
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:26,920
so

409
00:29:31,300 --> 00:29:34,420
much for watching.

410
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:41,900
Thank you.
